{# Shared <t inf> target-marking rules. Set `voice = true` before including for themed prompts. #}
## Target markup (required)

Wrap the target word or phrase — in whatever inflected form appears — in `<t inf="...">...</t>` tags in every example sentence.{% if voice %} The target stays in the sentence regardless of voice, so cloze and highlight still work.{% endif %} Never emit an example without this markup.

`inf` must be exactly one of:
- `base` — base form (glisten, run, cat)
- `past` — past simple (glistened, ran)
- `past_participle` — past participle (run, as in "has run")
- `present_3sg` — third-person singular present (glistens, runs)
- `ing` — -ing form (glistening, running)
- `plural` — plural noun (cats)
- `comparative` — comparative (happier)
- `superlative` — superlative (happiest)

Pick the `inf` matching the form actually used in the sentence; when word forms are listed, draw from those surfaces. Tag each part of a multi-word target separately.

Examples:
- "The snow <t inf="past">glistened</t> in the morning light."
- "Her eyes <t inf="base">glisten</t> with tears."
- Phrase "bring up": "She <t inf="past">brought</t> the children <t inf="base">up</t> alone."